From 7b33905397ece095c0844313c90a8716d66bf1f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:54:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkcif: Feed the RV1126 ISP with raw frames

The VICAP of the RV1126 has no IOMMU, so the raw frames it shares with
the ISP are allocated by its video node, and the ISP readback takes
MSB-justified 16-bit words.

Offer unpacked RAW10 and RAW12 samples written MSB-justified, with the
high alignment bit, as the 16-bit Bayer formats. One 16-bit format
serves two bus codes, so the capture picks the format by the bus code
as well, and the enumeration lists each format once unless it is asked
for one bus code. Offer the MIPI stream to a consumer through a V4L2
subdevice described by rkcif-toisp.h, so that the ISP driver can take
every completed frame.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
